{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe completion verifier's step budget routinely exhausts on legitimate validation work, failing criteria as \"unmet\" that are merely unproven-within-budget. Two epic closes hit this in one day (fb8a: request_limit=24 exhausted, 2 false unmets; the pony epic: repeated exhaustion across re-verifies, 5 then 1 false unmets), and the pressure drives operators/agents toward attestation-laundering.\n\n## Design intent (operator-stated, canonical)\nThe ONLY goal of the budget floor is to prevent runaway tool use that spends tokens without delivering a result. For VALID tool use the floor must be GENEROUS and the scaling must give ample room to validate complex ACs. We optimize against runaway, never to artificially limit authorized validation.\n\n## Current mechanics (completion.py, completion_banking.py, completion_recovery.py)\n`verify_step_floor(c) = clamp(steps_per_criterion x c, step_floor_min, 480)` with defaults 8/48; structured_run halves steps into pydantic-ai request_limit. A 6-AC epic gets the floor: 48 steps = 24 requests. Defects vs intent:\n1. Story-calibrated cost model: 8 steps/criterion assumes repo-file evidence; epic criteria traverse child tickets (show_ticket + comments + repo reads, 5-10 requests each) plus fixed overhead (initial show_ticket, description parse). No evidence-surface term.\n2. Runaway is ALREADY separately guarded (tool_calls_limit in-turn backstop, run_failure loop/repeat detection, the 480 clamp), so a small budget adds no safety — only false FAILs.\n3. No cross-run carryover: every re-verify re-proves all criteria from scratch (whack-a-mole loops, ~10 min each).\n\n## Plan\n1. Raise defaults: completion_verify_steps_per_criterion 8 -> 24, completion_verify_step_floor_min 48 -> 160 (matches the interim user-config mitigation deployed on the operator machine, which this change supersedes). Reconsider the 480 clamp: raise to 960 so 24/criterion scales usefully past 20 ACs — the clamp is a runaway ceiling, not a validation cap.\n2. Evidence-surface-aware scaling: budget = per_criterion x c + child_traversal x direct_children (epics/parents) + fixed_overhead. Children counted from the ticket graph at budget-sizing time (same place criteria_count is computed).\n3. Cross-run PASS-verdict cache (a NEW ticket-scoped store; the existing `CriterionBank` in completion_banking.py:396-435 stays run-scoped EXACTLY as designed — its run-unique dir exists so concurrent closes cannot collide, and this plan preserves that invariant, it does not reverse it). A separate cache at `.rebar/cache/completion_verdicts/<ticket>/<criterion-hash>.json`, written ONLY on a validated PASS record at finalize (atomic tmp+rename; concurrent same-ticket writers last-write-wins on identical keys — safe because entries are validated-PASS-only and keyed by content). Invalidation granularity: NOT the whole-repo HEAD tree sha (`_resolve_tree_sha`, completion_banking.py:358-373 — any unrelated commit would rotate it and defeat reuse); key each entry by (criterion-text hash, scoped material fingerprint) where the scoped fingerprint reuses the existing `BankStamps`/`resolve_bank_stamps` seam (:358-392) narrowed to the blobs under the ticket's file_impact paths; when own file_impact is empty but the ticket has children (the epic case — the highest-value reuse target), the fingerprint is the union of direct-child file_impact blobs (the `_subtree_impacts` seam); the whole-tree sha is the fallback ONLY for childless tickets with empty file_impact. Credit-vs-evaluate protocol: cache entries store the FULL banked record (met, evidence text, citations) from the original validated PASS; at run start (completion_recovery.py:487 `CriterionBank.for_run`) still-valid entries are SEEDED into the run's CriterionBank verbatim, so the bounded search targets only unproven criteria. Finalizer interaction (completion_verifier_finalizer.md:23-25 rules 'missing evidence must be met:false' / 'copy only citations present in the evidence'): the seeded record's own evidence+citations ride into the finalizer payload exactly as a same-run banked record's do, so the finalizer judges complete evidence, and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` (bank = source of truth post-1788) re-stamps any finalizer downgrade of a seeded record back from the bank — a seeded credit cannot be silently lost to prompt conservatism; RED test: finalizer echo that drops a seeded criterion still yields the credited verdict. Exhaustion then converges across runs. (Marker semantics from 1d71-a76c-04f6-4642 apply: cached entries are PASS-only; insufficiency is never cached.)\n4. Keep runaway guards authoritative: tool_calls_limit + loop detection unchanged; document in completion.py that the budget exists ONLY for runaway prevention.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Defaults raised (24 / 160; clamp 960) with the rationale documented at verify_step_floor; a 6-AC epic sizes to >=80 requests and a 15-AC epic to >=180; unit tests on the formula, INCLUDING updating the hard-coded pins in tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py (verify_step_floor(1)==48, (8)==64, (40)==320, (100)==480, captured max_iterations==48, and the _VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX==480 pin) to the new 24/160/960 mechanics.\n- [ ] Budget sizing adds a child-traversal term for tickets with direct children, tested with an epic fixture (childful ticket sizes strictly larger than a childless one at equal criteria count).\n- [ ] A re-verify after budget exhaustion credits still-valid cached PASS verdicts (same scoped fingerprint + criterion text) by seeding them into the run-scoped CriterionBank, and spends budget only on unproven criteria; invalidation on scoped-fingerprint or text change is RED->GREEN; an unrelated commit outside file_impact does NOT invalidate; the run-scoped bank's concurrent-close isolation is regression-tested.\n- [ ] Runaway protection regression-guarded: tool_calls_limit and loop detection behavior unchanged (existing tests still pass); a looping-tool fixture still trips the backstop under the larger budget.\n- [ ] `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786743539632916001,"uuid":"182c417a-4c08-40bc-9fe4-f14cec33373f"}